on concern for  repercussions concern for criticism that  really has all gone away i've seen a lot  of people standing up saying what they  believe and whatever the repercussions  are they are how has it felt for you  personally has it felt like there's a  weight off of you that allows you to say  what you believe when you believe it  uh no i don't think that none of that  really bothered me i think this is just  the timing of the letter i don't think  uh me uh feeling pressured to be able to  speak my mind or anything had to do with  the letter uh or about i do agree with  you it has gave people more chance to be  to speak their mind or be uh to to be  more open about these type of things and  uh  for me i just i just try to not be  distracted  uh just always try to preach love on  people  um unity uh because  uh you can get caught up in uh you can  get caught up and distracted on what's  going on on tv what's going on in the  news  and um and really that take over what's  going on and really take over your mind  so i just try to have a clear mind clear  focus  and just always preach love  and that's what i try to do  you mentioned coach lin's leadership  chris and he's been outspoken about some  of the things he believes some of the  interviews he's done what kinds of  messages has he given directly to the  team about getting through this  difficult time and and getting closer as  a team getting closer as a community and  understanding the the issues that exist  as we try to to make those issues not  issues anymore yeah  oh yeah we had a long hour talk with  coach lynn and he addressed uh  i think he he addressed each group each  position group and  he addresses that as a team  and uh that's what you have to do as a  coach man you have to put everything out  there i think  and  know that you're in tune with the world  know that telling your players you're  into what's going on with the world and  that you feel that you have compassion  with that and when you do that with your  players uh your player is going to write  a dot for you and and that's what he's  done he's been able to show compassion  uh with the situation and and with us  and uh when you do that man um that's  huge that's huge for players  went back to the decision to join the  chargers and this may have come up when  we got together at the super bowl but  you had your chance to get away from  patrick mahomes what are you thinking  staying in the division with patrick  mahomes chris  hey man  you gotta love competition man i've  never been a guy that ran from  competition and uh they're the best  right now they were super bowl champs uh  i know what it feels like to be the  champ after that next year is hard it's  hard to it's hard to duplicate that same  results and uh so uh i mean  everybody's the championship is up for  grabs it's a whole new year and you  gotta prove yourself again  the uh  the chargers have i think one of the  best defenses in the nfl  what stands out to you when you think  about those new teammates knowing that  you came from a team that not long ago  had one of the best defenses of all time  yeah  uh being able to play with all those  guys i mean  one thing i really noticed is that these  guys are already established i mean they  already got pro bowls all pros and me  just joining those guys is just going to  me i'm trying to boost their play try to  um try to raise their game into another  level and  and uh with my knowledge that i have  within the division and just being a  successful player on the field and when  i see darwin james i mean i haven't  played with anybody as talented as  darwin james other than i would say keep  to leave or uh i played with the ladder  and the champ bailey but nobody like  darren james how you can mess up the  game in the secondary so i'm excited  about playing with him uh bosa and  ingram those guys are they they kind of  give me familiarity with vine and d ware  or vine and doomerville how they used to 